# Job: node — root cause of the "lost first reply" that `285cfa522a` (half-budget replay) papered over; align replay with the new spec

You are a codex sub-agent under a Claude supervisor. Read `AGENTS.md` (root) §2/§3/§4.1 and `framework/AGENTS.md`. Never modify `core/**`, `bindings/**`, any `doc/spec/**`, `framework/doc/framework/**`, `doc/site/**`, other languages' trees; never lower an assertion; do not commit. Root-cause rule (user mandate): no budget/timeout increases, no retries "to be safe", no fixture changes that hide runtime behaviour; if the honest fix makes a test fail or slow, report it with evidence instead of mitigating. Do not rebuild Core or local packages. B session owns Core/bindings — if you find a Core/binding defect, STOP that item and report it with a public-API repro description. Env: `framework/languages/node`, `TMPDIR=/dev/shm/zlink-tmp-node`, `unset ZLINK_LIBRARY_PATH`, `flock -w7200 /tmp/zlink-node-gate.lock` around every npm/test invocation. Another node job edits `scripts/run_node_runtime_gate.js` and `samples/SupportChat.Ts/**` concurrently — do not touch those.

## Facts
- `285cfa522a` changed `packages/framework/src/runtime/foundation/service-stateful-runtime.ts` (~:4008-4017) so a durable operation's first attempt gets only half of the remaining deadline, to leave room for a terminal replay after the first reply was lost in `test/contract/user-spot-native-two-process.test.js`. Review verdict (`review-campaign-cpp-node.md`, row `285cfa522a` + 재수정 권고 2): C — the LOSS of the first reply is the unexplained root cause; the half split forces slow-but-healthy first attempts to abort and retries every error.
- The spec now defines the sender policy (`framework/doc/framework/common/spec/server/03-spot-actor/04-actor-model.ko.md`, the four new bullets after "Terminal record가 original deadline 뒤 5분…"): only durable lifecycle operations replay with the same OperationId; on any outcome WITHOUT a terminal envelope (missing route, the single handover timeout, lost reply); each attempt uses the WHOLE remaining deadline (no split); no attempt limit; DeadlineExceeded at exhaustion; application requests never replay. Also Core socket README §4: a request admitted on the losing direction of a reciprocal HANDOVER times out exactly once and the caller resends.

## What to do
1. Reproduce the two-process User Spot scenario with the half split temporarily neutralised (use the whole deadline) and capture ONE timeline per run (5×): flow_id/correlation of the first attempt, target-side terminal record write time, which physical pair/direction the reply used, HANDOVER winner/loser and their retire times (monitor events), and the binding REQUEST terminal the sender observed. Decide: (a) the target executed and the reply was lost on a retired pair (HANDOVER single timeout → expected by Core §4 → replay per spec is the right fix), or (b) the target never received it (route not yet admitted → NOT_CONNECTED → replay per spec), or (c) something else (a reply dropped while the pair is alive → Core/binding defect → STOP and report with the timeline).
2. Implement the spec policy in the node runtime: replay only for durable operations, only when no terminal envelope was received, whole remaining deadline per attempt, no split constant; compare with cpp's replay path (`framework/languages/cpp/framework/src/runtime/**` route/retry) for parity and note any cpp divergence from the new spec in the report (do not edit cpp).
3. Regression: a contract test that pins "first attempt is not cut short" (a healthy first attempt that takes >50% of the deadline completes) and "replay after a lost reply uses the same OperationId and completes within the original deadline". Run the two-process test 5×, the replay-related contract tests, and `node --test` on the touched test files.

## Deliverable
`doc/plan/c016-worklog/stage1-node-first-reply-loss-summary.md`: timeline table (5 runs), classification (a/b/c) with evidence, diff, regression, results, cpp parity note, BLOCKERS.
